Looking at the symbol validation for the Framework parameter, the type and datatype are both defined, and the description is there. The choice datatype has its options properly defined and non-empty. The defaultValue "net9.0" matches one of the available choices, so that's valid too.

The choices are formatted as an object keyed by value rather than an array of objects, but both formats work fine in the template engine. There's only one parameter, so no prefix collisions to worry about. Sources, post-actions, and constraints aren't defined, so nothing to validate there. The tags for language and type are both present.

The template only needs two minor suggestions—adding a description and a defaultName—but otherwise it's solid and ready to go.
